{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"07b89898-5b1d-4a67-863b-b3b702fb2881","agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (FastAPI cuore/). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no commits, no Edge, no code changes except the new doc and one test. Report under 80 words. Other agents are editing mobile templates, vision_bridge, media API: only read them.\n\nProduce docs/mobile/API_CONTRACT.md: the contract a native iPhone app (Swift or Flutter) will consume to replace the web page /m/{vin}. Generate it from the running schema: with CUORE_STATE_DIR set to a temp dir, create the app (cuore.app.create_app) and read app.openapi(); include every path under /api/owner, /api/vision (may not exist yet; if absent, document the contract as specified in cuore/services/vision_bridge.py's docstring or note \"pending\"), /api/media (upload, list, fetch), /api/health, and the vehicle identity endpoint the mobile page uses. For each: method, path, params, request body shape, response shape with an example, error codes. Then sections: authentication (none today; loopback or trusted LAN only; what a native app must add before leaving the LAN), attested-record semantics (confidence \"reported\", fields_meta \"photo\", never car measurements), remembered values (recents), idempotency, image upload limits and HEIC note, and a \"native-only features\" list (Location Services → station field, camera capture → /api/vision read, push for /api/owner messages). Add cuore/tests/check_api_contract.py that fails if any path listed in the doc disappears from app.openapi() (parse the doc's path table). Run it."},"uuid":"0f56fcd8-e950-4f68-b076-2ec97c1f7568","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:55:49.242Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
