D","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"a2acdf42-8dac-4fc3-8a25-2c7a3d96cd4a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4da60c7b-27b0-40d1-b6d9-a9af782d7870","agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YQ1iJgKPmxn9ECkqVpCPaT","type":"tool_result","content":"14-6. Port to Maserati and Ferrari: module maps and DID catalogues keyed by platform, VIN decoding for ZN6/ZN7, spec tables per model, brand accent as a theme variable, experience and parts tables per marque. Keep the Stelvio data as the template.\n15-7. Hygiene: fix `electrical_inspections.latest()` (newest record), the clipped \"...\" strip button at 400 px, and keep agent tests to 4-5 checks each.\n16-\n17-## Mobile companion (decided 2026-10-13)\n18-\n19:The phone surface \"Tell CUORE\" (/m/{vin}) records what the car cannot tell us (fluids, fuel and octane, battery and electrical work, tyres, parts fitted elsewhere, exposure, incidents, driving pattern) as attested records, and carries messages between owner, mechanic and CUORE. Standard: the same prestige as the main app (dark, one statement per screen, pictograms, red for the one action), opening reveal on every open, a fill-up recordable in three taps, a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump proposing the fields for the human to confirm (pluggable vision provider, off by default because CUORE runs offline; the Claude provider is an explicit opt-in that sends the photo to Anthropic).\n20-\n21:Native app path (owner has an Apple developer account and Xcode): the web page is the reference implementation and the JSON API under /api/owner, /api/vision, /api/media is the contract a Flutter or Swift app talks to. Features that need the phone itself (Location Services for the station, background capture, a \"pull up to the pump\" shortcut, push for messages) belong to the native app; nothing in the web surface should block that, so all logic stays server-side behind the API and the page keeps no state of its own.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"29bf59c9-8fc8-45ea-a809-a6f148ef4a34","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:57:10.064Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"14-6. Port to Maserati and Ferrari: module maps and DID catalogues keyed by platform, VIN decoding for ZN6/ZN7, spec tables per model, brand accent as a theme variable, experience and parts tables per marque. Keep the Stelvio data as the template.\n15-7. Hygiene: fix `electrical_inspections.latest()` (newest record), the clipped \"...\" strip button at 400 px, and keep agent tests to 4-5 checks each.\n16-\n17-## Mobile companion (decided 2026-10-13)\n18-\n19:The phone surface \"Tell CUORE\" (/m/{vin}) records what the car cannot tell us (fluids, fuel and octane, battery and electrical work, tyres, parts fitted elsewhere, exposure, incidents, driving pattern) as attested records, and carries messages between owner, mechanic and CUORE. Standard: the same prestige as the main app (dark, one statement per screen, pictograms, red for the one action), opening reveal on every open, a fill-up recordable in three taps, a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump proposing the fields for the human to confirm (pluggable vision provider, off by default because CUORE runs offline; the Claude provider is an explicit opt-in that sends the photo to Anthropic).\n20-\n21:Native app path (owner has an Apple developer account and Xcode): the web page is the reference implementation and the JSON API under /api/owner, /api/vision, /api/media is the contract a Flutter or Swift app talks to. Features that need the phone itself (Location Services for the station, background capture, a \"pull up to the pump\" shortcut, push for messages) belong to the native app; nothing in the web surface should block that, so all logic stays server-side behind the API and the page keeps no state of its own.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5ccb16a2-a57c-48d0-bd46-439abeb0736c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2acdf42-8dac-4fc3-8a25-2c7a3d96cd4a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"145cfa11-a1be-414f-917a-d276c75c165d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4da60c7b-27b0-40d1-b6d9-a9af782d7870","agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U5e9uKDCAizuMQ89m5yDdt","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:185:1. **One process for the adapter.** Recommend cuore owns COM3 and `obd2-mcp` imports `cuore.live` in-process. The alternative, `obd2-mcp` calling cuore over HTTP, is cleaner for concurrency but adds a running service dependency to every Claude session.\ndocs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:186:2. **Cable declaration UX.** A tool call and an HTTP route are proposed. A physical alternative is to read the bus passively on every open and infer the cable from traffic rate and IDs; that is safer but slower, and is worth adding once the buses are verified.\ndocs/handbook/06-roadmap.md:17:## Mobile companion (decided 2026-10-13)\ndocs/handbook/06-roadmap.md:21:Native app path (owner has an Apple developer account and Xcode): the web page is the reference implementation and the JSON API under /api/owner, /api/vision, /api/media is the contract a Flutter or Swift app talks to. Features that need the phone itself (Location Services for the station, background capture, a \"pull up to the pump\" shortcut, push for messages) belong to the native app; nothing in the web surface should block that, so all logic stays server-side behind the API and the page keeps no state of its own.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9fa7a246-f32d-42a9-b130-481d96d65e7f","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:57:10.091Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:185:1. **One process for the adapter.** Recommend cuore owns COM3 and `obd2-mcp` imports `cuore.live` in-process. The alternative, `obd2-mcp` calling cuore over HTTP, is cleaner for concurrency but adds a running service dependency to every Claude session.\ndocs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:186:2. **Cable declaration UX.** A tool call and an HTTP route are proposed. A physical alternative is to read the bus passively on every open and infer the cable from traffic rate and IDs; that is safer but slower, and is worth adding once the buses are verified.\ndocs/handbook/06-roadmap.md:17:## Mobile companion (decided 2026-10-13)\ndocs/handbook/06-roadmap.md:21:Native app path (owner has an Apple developer account and Xcode): the web page is the reference implementation and the JSON API under /api/owner, /api/vision, /api/media is the contract a Flutter or Swift app talks to. Features that need the phone itself (Location Services for the station, background capture, a \"pull up to the pump\" shortcut, push for messages) belong to the native app; nothing in the web surface should block that, so all logic stays server-side behind the API and the page keeps no state of its own.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5ccb16a2-a57c-48d0-bd46-439abeb0736c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"145cfa11-a1be-414f-917a-d276c75c165d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
