{"parentUuid":"76daf3e2-f987-4e61-a70a-6abc0ee2ac09","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"32e1d820-4c02-417b-9eb5-eb28de0dd113","agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015C1QoWShqnxPsyxQHr43ma","type":"tool_result","content":"``mes.symptoms`` (via :mod:`cuore.services.timeline_bridge`), the store the\nmechanic-vs-driver timeline already reads, so the same report shows up in\nboth places instead of forking into a second, drifting copy. See\n:mod:`cuore.services.owner_events_bridge` for where that hand-off happens.\n\nAppend-only JSONL under ``cuore.live.config.state_dir()`` (``CUORE_STATE_DIR``,\nsame precedence as every other cuore live store), one file,\n``owner_events.jsonl``, two record shapes distinguished by ``op``:\n\n* ``event`` -- {op, id, vin, at, recorded_at, by: {role, name}, category,\n  kind, fields, fields_meta, note, media_ids, odometer_km, confidence=\"reported\"}\n* ``delete``-- {op, id, at} -- marks an event hidden (soft delete)\n\n``fields_meta`` (added 2026-10-13, additive -- older rows simply have none)\nis ``{field_key: \"photo\"}`` for any field whose value was read off a photo\nby the Mobile \"Snap & fill\" screen (``cuore.web.owner_routes``) rather than\ntyped by the person -- see that module's own docstring for the contract\nwith ``cuore.services.vision_bridge``. It is informational only: a\nphoto-read field is stored at the same ``confidence: \"reported\"`` as every\nother owner-typed value (a human still tapped Save), this just remembers\n*how* the value got into the box, for the \"check before saving\" amber chip\n---\n            row = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n        if isinstance(row, dict):\n            out.append(row)\n    return out\n\n\ndef kind_def(category: str, kind: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Raises ``ValueError`` if ``category``/``kind`` is not in :data:`TAXONOMY`.\"\"\"\n    cat = TAXONOMY.get(category)\n    if cat is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unknown category {category!r}; use one of: \"\n                         + \", \".join(TAXONOMY))\n    kd = cat[\"kinds\"].get(kind)\n    if kd is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unknown kind {kind!r} for category {category!r}; use one of: \"\n                         + \", \".join(cat[\"kinds\"]))\n    return kd\n\n\ndef _parse_iso_or_date(at: Optional[str]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"``at`` may be a full timestamp or a bare date; default is now.\"\"\"\n    s = (at or \"\").strip()\n    if not s:\n        return datetime.now().isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")\n    try:\n        datetime.fromisoformat(s)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"at must be an ISO date or timestamp, got {at!r}\") from exc\n    return s\n\n\ndef add(vin: str, category: str, kind: str, *, at: Optional[str] = None,\n        by_role: str = \"owner\", by_name: str = \"\", fields: Optional[dict[str, Any]] = None,\n        note: str = \"\", media_ids: Optional[list[str]] = None,\n        odometer_km: Optional[float] = None,\n        fields_meta: Optional[dict[str, str]] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Validate against :data:`TAXONOMY`, stamp and append one owner-event\n    row. Raises ``ValueError`` on anything the API layer should turn into a\n    400: unknown category/kind, bad role, bad timestamp, note too long.\n\n    ``fields`` is not type-checked field-by-field beyond stringifying and\n    length-capping each value -- the taxonomy's per-kind field list is a\n    form/display contract, not a second validation gate; the one thing this\n    function enforces strictly is that the category/kind itself exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n    if not vin:\n        raise ValueError(\"vin is required\")\n    category = (category or \"\").strip()\n    kind = (kind or \"\").strip()\n    kind_def(category, kind)  # raises on unknown category/kind\n\n    by_role = (by_role or \"owner\").strip().lower()\n    if by_role not in BY_ROLES:\n        raise ValueError(\"by_role must be one of: \" + \", \".join(BY_ROLES))\n\n    at_v = _parse_iso_or_date(at)\n    note = (note or \"\").strip()\n    if len(note) > MAX_NOTE:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"db634f1d-f71b-4ea7-b692-d9fc5f50e9b8","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:01:50.580Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"``mes.symptoms`` (via :mod:`cuore.services.timeline_bridge`), the store the\nmechanic-vs-driver timeline already reads, so the same report shows up in\nboth places instead of forking into a second, drifting copy. See\n:mod:`cuore.services.owner_events_bridge` for where that hand-off happens.\n\nAppend-only JSONL under ``cuore.live.config.state_dir()`` (``CUORE_STATE_DIR``,\nsame precedence as every other cuore live store), one file,\n``owner_events.jsonl``, two record shapes distinguished by ``op``:\n\n* ``event`` -- {op, id, vin, at, recorded_at, by: {role, name}, category,\n  kind, fields, fields_meta, note, media_ids, odometer_km, confidence=\"reported\"}\n* ``delete``-- {op, id, at} -- marks an event hidden (soft delete)\n\n``fields_meta`` (added 2026-10-13, additive -- older rows simply have none)\nis ``{field_key: \"photo\"}`` for any field whose value was read off a photo\nby the Mobile \"Snap & fill\" screen (``cuore.web.owner_routes``) rather than\ntyped by the person -- see that module's own docstring for the contract\nwith ``cuore.services.vision_bridge``. It is informational only: a\nphoto-read field is stored at the same ``confidence: \"reported\"`` as every\nother owner-typed value (a human still tapped Save), this just remembers\n*how* the value got into the box, for the \"check before saving\" amber chip\n---\n            row = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n        if isinstance(row, dict):\n            out.append(row)\n    return out\n\n\ndef kind_def(category: str, kind: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Raises ``ValueError`` if ``category``/``kind`` is not in :data:`TAXONOMY`.\"\"\"\n    cat = TAXONOMY.get(category)\n    if cat is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unknown category {category!r}; use one of: \"\n                         + \", \".join(TAXONOMY))\n    kd = cat[\"kinds\"].get(kind)\n    if kd is None:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unknown kind {kind!r} for category {category!r}; use one of: \"\n                         + \", \".join(cat[\"kinds\"]))\n    return kd\n\n\ndef _parse_iso_or_date(at: Optional[str]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"``at`` may be a full timestamp or a bare date; default is now.\"\"\"\n    s = (at or \"\").strip()\n    if not s:\n        return datetime.now().isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")\n    try:\n        datetime.fromisoformat(s)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"at must be an ISO date or timestamp, got {at!r}\") from exc\n    return s\n\n\ndef add(vin: str, category: str, kind: str, *, at: Optional[str] = None,\n        by_role: str = \"owner\", by_name: str = \"\", fields: Optional[dict[str, Any]] = None,\n        note: str = \"\", media_ids: Optional[list[str]] = None,\n        odometer_km: Optional[float] = None,\n        fields_meta: Optional[dict[str, str]] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Validate against :data:`TAXONOMY`, stamp and append one owner-event\n    row. Raises ``ValueError`` on anything the API layer should turn into a\n    400: unknown category/kind, bad role, bad timestamp, note too long.\n\n    ``fields`` is not type-checked field-by-field beyond stringifying and\n    length-capping each value -- the taxonomy's per-kind field list is a\n    form/display contract, not a second validation gate; the one thing this\n    function enforces strictly is that the category/kind itself exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n    if not vin:\n        raise ValueError(\"vin is required\")\n    category = (category or \"\").strip()\n    kind = (kind or \"\").strip()\n    kind_def(category, kind)  # raises on unknown category/kind\n\n    by_role = (by_role or \"owner\").strip().lower()\n    if by_role not in BY_ROLES:\n        raise ValueError(\"by_role must be one of: \" + \", \".join(BY_ROLES))\n\n    at_v = _parse_iso_or_date(at)\n    note = (note or \"\").strip()\n    if len(note) > MAX_NOTE:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0919a0bc-0f19-4e69-adae-a923f783e5b9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"76daf3e2-f987-4e61-a70a-6abc0ee2ac09","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
