edia item (soft delete) |","+| GET | /api/vision/status | Which photo-reading provider is configured |","+| POST | /api/vision/{vin}/read | Read one photo (odometer, fuel pump, oil bottle, part label, or receipt) |"," ","-`/api/vision/*` is **not** in this table -- it does not exist in the running","-schema yet. See [Vision (pending)](#vision-pending) below for the contract","-to build to once it lands.","+`/api/vision/*` landed mid-write of this document (it did not exist at the","+start of this pass; `cuore/services/vision_bridge.py` and `cuore/api/vision.py`","+were built concurrently by another agent). See [Vision](#vision) below for","+the real contract, captured from the live schema rather than the \"pending\"","+placeholder this section originally held."," "," ---"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0bc16661-4560-403e-9ce9-79255361a1f3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4b886cbb-e2cc-4dea-8981-37423c8ae637","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"07eef59c-f4b3-4d89-9efb-3fd48e8f0731","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14842862 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"87d8670e-e6d7-4b62-b00e-6e31fc2b9cbd","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:02:26.909Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14842862 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"87d8670e-e6d7-4b62-b00e-6e31fc2b9cbd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01DWNPPUSsd4GdBUpnmUgtZM","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f0f7d319-485d-493c-a6c5-b90962fd7cb5","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:02:57.538Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"f0f7d319-485d-493c-a6c5-b90962fd7cb5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfzuro3xMqhzyDrtUKfrp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TYL6PFcsiJJLwDM19Wbcd5","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md","old_string":"## Vision (pending)\n\n`/api/vision/*` **does not exist in the running schema** as of this\ndocument. It is specified, not built -- `docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md`\n(\"Mobile companion\", 2026-10-13):\n\n> a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump proposing the fields for the\n> human to confirm (pluggable vision provider, off by default because CUORE\n> runs offline; the Claude provider is an explicit opt-in that sends the\n> photo to Anthropic).\n\n`cuore/services/vision_bridge.py` does not exist yet either -- there is no\ndocstring to transcribe. The contract a native app should build against,\nonce it lands, follows the same shape as every other bridge in this file:\n\n* **Provider is pluggable and off by default.** CUORE runs offline; no\n  photo leaves the device/LAN unless a vision provider is explicitly\n  configured. The documented provider is Claude, and selecting it is an\n  explicit opt-in because it sends the photo to Anthropic.\n* **Proposes, never commits.** The expected flow is upload a photo (via the\n  existing `POST /api/vehicles/{vin}/media`, `target_kind` likely\n  `\"vehicle\"` or a new `target_kind` for pump/odometer/bottle shots), then\n  call a vision endpoint that returns *proposed field values* (e.g.\n  `{\"odometer_km\": 142290, \"confidence\": \"proposed\"}`) for a human to\n  confirm or correct before anything is written to `owner_events`. It must\n  not call `POST /api/owner/{vin}/events` itself -- the human-confirm step\n  stays a distinct request, same as every other attested record in this\n  system (see [attested-record semantics](#attested-record-semantics)).\n* **Native app implication:** until this ships, camera capture on a native\n  app has nothing to call for auto-fill -- see\n  [native-only features](#native-only-features). Treat this section as the\n  spec to implement against, and re-run\n  `cuore/tests/check_api_contract.py` once `/api/vision/*` exists; it will\n  not fail for vision's absence (vision is not in the path table above),\n  but this document's \"pending\" language should be updated to match\n  whatever `app.openapi()` then reports.","new_string":"## Vision\n\n`/api/vision/*` is live. HTTP face of `cuore.services.vision_bridge`\n(\"pluggable 'read this photo' service for the mobile 'Tell CUORE' page\"),\nmatching the roadmap note in `docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md` (\"Mobile\ncompanion\", 2026-10-13): *\"a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump\nproposing the fields for the human to confirm (pluggable vision provider,\noff by default because CUORE runs offline; the Claude provider is an\nexplicit opt-in that sends the photo to Anthropic).\"*\n\n**Every value this returns is a suggestion, never a measurement, never\nwritten automatically.** This module never calls `POST\n/api/owner/{vin}/events` itself -- it only reads a photo already in hand\n(upload it separately via the media API if it should also be kept as\nevidence) and proposes field values for a human to confirm in the add-event\nform.\n\n### `GET /api/vision/status`\n\nWhich provider is configured, and whether it can actually be used *right\nnow* -- never whether the last read succeeded.\n\n**Response 200** (default, no provider configured):\n\n```json\n{\"provider\": \"none\", \"available\": false, \"model\": null}\n```\n\nThree possible `provider` values: `\"none\"` (the default -- CUORE runs\noffline by rule; `available` is always `false`), `\"claude\"` (`available`\nreflects whether `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set server-side -- the photo is\nthen sent to Anthropic's Messages API over the open internet, an explicit\nopt-in the owner turns on via `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude`, never the\ndefault), `\"tesseract\"` (a documented hook; always `available: false`\ntoday -- no OCR binary is wired up).\n\n### `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`\n\n**Params:** `vin` (path, accepted but not used to scope the read).\n**Body:** `multipart/form-data` -- `file` (the photo, required) and `hint`\n(form field, required, one of `odometer | fuel_pump | oil_bottle |\npart_label | receipt | other`).\n\n**Response 200**, provider `\"none\"` (today's default -- this is what a\nnative app gets until an owner opts in to a provider):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"provider\": \"none\",\n  \"available\": false,\n  \"fields\": {},\n  \"suggested_kind\": null,\n  \"note\": \"Automatic reading is not set up on this CUORE. Fill in by hand.\"\n}\n```\n\nWith `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude` configured and a successful read, the\nshape (per-hint field set, from `vision_bridge._FIELD_SPECS`) is:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"provider\": \"claude\",\n  \"available\": true,\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"odometer_km\": {\"value\": 142290, \"confidence\": 0.9, \"unit\": \"km\"}\n  },\n  \"suggested_kind\": null,\n  \"note\": \"Suggested from the photo -- confirm or correct every field before saving; this is not a car measurement.\"\n}\n```\n\nPer-hint field names and `suggested_kind` (the taxonomy `category/kind` the\nnative app should pre-select, or `null` when there is no single matching\none):\n\n| hint | fields | suggested_kind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `odometer` | `odometer_km` (number, km) | `null` -- goes on the event's own `odometer_km`, not a `fields` entry |\n| `fuel_pump` | `litres`, `price`, `octane`, `station` | `fuel/fill_up` |\n| `oil_bottle` | `brand`, `viscosity`, `qty` | `fluids/engine_oil_change` |\n| `part_label` | `part`, `part_no`, `brand` | `parts_repairs_elsewhere/part_fitted_elsewhere` |\n| `receipt` | `station`, `litres`, `price`, `at` | `fuel/fill_up` |\n| `other` | provider's best effort, unshaped | `null` |\n\nEach field value is `{\"value\": <reading or null>, \"confidence\": 0.0-1.0,\n\"unit\": <ours, never the model's, or null>}` -- a native app should treat\n`value: null` or low `confidence` as \"show the field empty, let the human\ntype it,\" never auto-accept.\n\n**Errors:** `400` for an unrecognised `hint` --\n\n```json\n{\"detail\": \"hint must be one of odometer, fuel_pump, oil_bottle, part_label, receipt, other, got 'bogus'\"}\n```\n\nA failed Claude call (network/HTTP error, or a non-JSON reply) is **not**\nan HTTP error -- it still returns `200` with `available: false` (or\n`available: true, fields: {}` for an unparseable reply) and a human-\nreadable `note`. A native app must branch on `available`/`fields`, not on\nHTTP status, to detect \"nothing to suggest.\"\n\n### Gap: `fields_meta` provenance is not yet wired to the API\n\n`cuore.live.owner_events.add()` now accepts a `fields_meta:\ndict[str, \"photo\"]` parameter (added 2026-10-13) that records, per field,\nwhether its value came from a photo read rather than being typed --\n`cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.add()` passes it straight through. **But\n`POST /api/owner/{vin}/events`'s request body (`OwnerEventRequest` in\n`cuore/api/owner_events.py`) has no `fields_meta` field yet** -- confirmed\nagainst the live schema (`components.schemas.OwnerEventRequest` in\n`app.openapi()` has no such property). A native app cannot, today, tell the\nserver \"this value came from a vision read\" when it saves the event; that\nprovenance is currently only reachable from the yet-to-be-updated web\n\"Snap & fill\" flow at the `cuore.web.owner_routes` layer, not the JSON API.\nRe-check this once `check_api_contract.py`'s next run shows\n`OwnerEventRequest` growing a `fields_meta` property, and update this gap\nnote (and the request example in [owner events](#owner-events-tell-cuore))\naccordingly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":709,"cache_read_input_tokens":156531,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":709,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TYL6PFcsiJJLwDM19Wbcd5":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md","old_string":"## Vision (pending)\n\n`/api/vision/*` **does not exist in the running schema** as of this\ndocument. It is specified, not built -- `docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md`\n(\"Mobile companion\", 2026-10-13):\n\n> a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump proposing the fields for the\n> human to confirm (pluggable vision provider, off by default because CUORE\n> runs offline; the Claude provider is an explicit opt-in that sends the\n> photo to Anthropic).\n\n`cuore/services/vision_bridge.py` does not exist yet either -- there is no\ndocstring to transcribe. The contract a native app should build against,\nonce it lands, follows the same shape as every other bridge in this file:\n\n* **Provider is pluggable and off by default.** CUORE runs offline; no\n  photo leaves the device/LAN unless a vision provider is explicitly\n  configured. The documented provider is Claude, and selecting it is an\n  explicit opt-in because it sends the photo to Anthropic.\n* **Proposes, never commits.** The expected flow is upload a photo (via the\n  existing `POST /api/vehicles/{vin}/media`, `target_kind` likely\n  `\"vehicle\"` or a new `target_kind` for pump/odometer/bottle shots), then\n  call a vision endpoint that returns *proposed field values* (e.g.\n  `{\"odometer_km\": 142290, \"confidence\": \"proposed\"}`) for a human to\n  confirm or correct before anything is written to `owner_events`. It must\n  not call `POST /api/owner/{vin}/events` itself -- the human-confirm step\n  stays a distinct request, same as every other attested record in this\n  system (see [attested-record semantics](#attested-record-semantics)).\n* **Native app implication:** until this ships, camera capture on a native\n  app has nothing to call for auto-fill -- see\n  [native-only features](#native-only-features). Treat this section as the\n  spec to implement against, and re-run\n  `cuore/tests/check_api_contract.py` once `/api/vision/*` exists; it will\n  not fail for vision's absence (vision is not in the path table above),\n  but this document's \"pending\" language should be updated to match\n  whatever `app.openapi()` then reports.","new_string":"## Vision\n\n`/api/vision/*` is live. HTTP face of `cuore.services.vision_bridge`\n(\"pluggable 'read this photo' service for the mobile 'Tell CUORE' page\"),\nmatching the roadmap note in `docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md` (\"Mobile\ncompanion\", 2026-10-13): *\"a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump\nproposing the fields for the human to confirm (pluggable vision provider,\noff by default because CUORE runs offline; the Claude provider is an\nexplicit opt-in that sends the photo to Anthropic).\"*\n\n**Every value this returns is a suggestion, never a measurement, never\nwritten automatically.** This module never calls `POST\n/api/owner/{vin}/events` itself -- it only reads a photo already in hand\n(upload it separately via the media API if it should also be kept as\nevidence) and proposes field values for a human to confirm in the add-event\nform.\n\n### `GET /api/vision/status`\n\nWhich provider is configured, and whether it can actually be used *right\nnow* -- never whether the last read succeeded.\n\n**Response 200** (default, no provider configured):\n\n```json\n{\"provider\": \"none\", \"available\": false, \"model\": null}\n```\n\nThree possible `provider` values: `\"none\"` (the default -- CUORE runs\noffline by rule; `available` is always `false`), `\"claude\"` (`available`\nreflects whether `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set server-side -- the photo is\nthen sent to Anthropic's Messages API over the open internet, an explicit\nopt-in the owner turns on via `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude`, never the\ndefault), `\"tesseract\"` (a documented hook; always `available: false`\ntoday -- no OCR binary is wired up).\n\n### `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`\n\n**Params:** `vin` (path, accepted but not used to scope the read).\n**Body:** `multipart/form-data` -- `file` (the photo, required) and `hint`\n(form field, required, one of `odometer | fuel_pump | oil_bottle |\npart_label | receipt | other`).\n\n**Response 200**, provider `\"none\"` (today's default -- this is what a\nnative app gets until an owner opts in to a provider):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"provider\": \"none\",\n  \"available\": false,\n  \"fields\": {},\n  \"suggested_kind\": null,\n  \"note\": \"Automatic reading is not set up on this CUORE. Fill in by hand.\"\n}\n```\n\nWith `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude` configured and a successful read, the\nshape (per-hint field set, from `vision_bridge._FIELD_SPECS`) is:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"provider\": \"claude\",\n  \"available\": true,\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"odometer_km\": {\"value\": 142290, \"confidence\": 0.9, \"unit\": \"km\"}\n  },\n  \"suggested_kind\": null,\n  \"note\": \"Suggested from the photo -- confirm or correct every field before saving; this is not a car measurement.\"\n}\n```\n\nPer-hint field names and `suggested_kind` (the taxonomy `category/kind` the\nnative app should pre-select, or `null` when there is no single matching\none):\n\n| hint | fields | suggested_kind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `odometer` | `odometer_km` (number, km) | `null` -- goes on the event's own `odometer_km`, not a `fields` entry |\n| `fuel_pump` | `litres`, `price`, `octane`, `station` | `fuel/fill_up` |\n| `oil_bottle` | `brand`, `viscosity`, `qty` | `fluids/engine_oil_change` |\n| `part_label` | `part`, `part_no`, `brand` | `parts_repairs_elsewhere/part_fitted_elsewhere` |\n| `receipt` | `station`, `litres`, `price`, `at` | `fuel/fill_up` |\n| `other` | provider's best effort, unshaped | `null` |\n\nEach field value is `{\"value\": <reading or null>, \"confidence\": 0.0-1.0,\n\"unit\": <ours, never the model's, or null>}` -- a native app should treat\n`value: null` or low `confidence` as \"show the field empty, let the human\ntype it,\" never auto-accept.\n\n**Errors:** `400` for an unrecognised `hint` --\n\n```json\n{\"detail\": \"hint must be one of odometer, fuel_pump, oil_bottle, part_label, receipt, other, got 'bogus'\"}\n```\n\nA failed Claude call (network/HTTP error, or a non-JSON reply) is **not**\nan HTTP error -- it still returns `200` with `available: false` (or\n`available: true, fields: {}` for an unparseable reply) and a human-\nreadable `note`. A native app must branch on `available`/`fields`, not on\nHTTP status, to detect \"nothing to suggest.\"\n\n### Gap: `fields_meta` provenance is not yet wired to the API\n\n`cuore.live.owner_events.add()` now accepts a `fields_meta:\ndict[str, \"photo\"]` parameter (added 2026-10-13) that records, per field,\nwhether its value came from a photo read rather than being typed --\n`cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.add()` passes it straight through. **But\n`POST /api/owner/{vin}/events`'s request body (`OwnerEventRequest` in\n`cuore/api/owner_events.py`) has no `fields_meta` field yet** -- confirmed\nagainst the live schema (`components.schemas.OwnerEventRequest` in\n`app.openapi()` has no such property). A native app cannot, today, tell the\nserver \"this value came from a vision read\" when it saves the event; that\nprovenance is currently only reachable from the yet-to-be-updated web\n\"Snap & fill\" flow at the `cuore.web.owner_routes` layer, not the JSON API.\nRe-check this once `check_api_contract.py`'s next run shows\n`OwnerEventRequest` growing a `fields_meta` property, and update this gap\nnote (and the request example in [owner events](#owner-events-tell-cuore))\naccordingly."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"df8d92ae-ef42-4309-8679-cd086185a4de","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfzurnnpkJ46xLhEdiVGf","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"beddb72a-7313-4205-9912-b0b1db5d2020","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:02:57.537Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"beddb72a-7313-4205-9912-b0b1db5d2020","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"32e1d820-4c02-417b-9eb5-eb28de0dd113","agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TYL6PFcsiJJLwDM19Wbcd5","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"d7514432-703d-4184-bc56-76d2b6a9704d","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:02:58.269Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md","oldString":"## Vision (pending)\n\n`/api/vision/*` **does not exist in the running schema** as of this\ndocument. It is specified, not built -- `docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md`\n(\"Mobile companion\", 2026-10-13):\n\n> a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump proposing the fields for the\n> human to confirm (pluggable vision provider, off by default because CUORE\n> runs offline; the Claude provider is an explicit opt-in that sends the\n> photo to Anthropic).\n\n`cuore/services/vision_bridge.py` does not exist yet either -- there is no\ndocstring to transcribe. The contract a native app should build against,\nonce it lands, follows the same shape as every other bridge in this file:\n\n* **Provider is pluggable and off by default.** CUORE runs offline; no\n  photo leaves the device/LAN unless a vision provider is explicitly\n  configured. The documented provider is Claude, and selecting it is an\n  explicit opt-in because it sends the photo to Anthropic.\n* **Proposes, never commits.** The expected flow is upload a photo (via the\n  existing `POST /api/vehicles/{vin}/media`, `target_kind` likely\n  `\"vehicle\"` or a new `target_kind` for pump/odometer/bottle shots), then\n  call a vision endpoint that returns *proposed field values* (e.g.\n  `{\"odometer_km\": 142290, \"confidence\": \"proposed\"}`) for a human to\n  confirm or correct before anything is written to `owner_events`. It must\n  not call `POST /api/owner/{vin}/events` itself -- the human-confirm step\n  stays a distinct request, same as every other attested record in this\n  system (see [attested-record semantics](#attested-record-semantics)).\n* **Native app implication:** until this ships, camera capture on a native\n  app has nothing to call for auto-fill -- see\n  [native-only features](#native-only-features). Treat this section as the\n  spec to implement against, and re-run\n  `cuore/tests/check_api_contract.py` once `/api/vision/*` exists; it will\n  not fail for vision's absence (vision is not in the path table above),\n  but this document's \"pending\" language should be updated to match\n  whatever `app.openapi()` then reports.","newString":"## Vision\n\n`/api/vision/*` is live. HTTP face of `cuore.services.vision_bridge`\n(\"pluggable 'read this photo' service for the mobile 'Tell CUORE' page\"),\nmatching the roadmap note in `docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md` (\"Mobile\ncompanion\", 2026-10-13): *\"a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump\nproposing the fields for the human to confirm (pluggable vision provider,\noff by default because CUORE runs offline; the Claude provider is an\nexplicit opt-in that sends the photo to Anthropic).\"*\n\n**Every value this returns is a suggestion, never a measurement, never\nwritten automatically.** This module never calls `POST\n/api/owner/{vin}/events` itself -- it only reads a photo already in hand\n(upload it separately via the media API if it should also be kept as\nevidence) and proposes field values for a human to confirm in the add-event\nform.\n\n### `GET /api/vision/status`\n\nWhich provider is configured, and whether it can actually be used *right\nnow* -- never whether the last read succeeded.\n\n**Response 200** (default, no provider configured):\n\n```json\n{\"provider\": \"none\", \"available\": false, \"model\": null}\n```\n\nThree possible `provider` values: `\"none\"` (the default -- CUORE runs\noffline by rule; `available` is always `false`), `\"claude\"` (`available`\nreflects whether `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set server-side -- the photo is\nthen sent to Anthropic's Messages API over the open internet, an explicit\nopt-in the owner turns on via `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude`, never the\ndefault), `\"tesseract\"` (a documented hook; always `available: false`\ntoday -- no OCR binary is wired up).\n\n### `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`\n\n**Params:** `vin` (path, accepted but not used to scope the read).\n**Body:** `multipart/form-data` -- `file` (the photo, required) and `hint`\n(form field, required, one of `odometer | fuel_pump | oil_bottle |\npart_label | receipt | other`).\n\n**Response 200**, provider `\"none\"` (today's default -- this is what a\nnative app gets until an owner opts in to a provider):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"provider\": \"none\",\n  \"available\": false,\n  \"fields\": {},\n  \"suggested_kind\": null,\n  \"note\": \"Automatic reading is not set up on this CUORE. Fill in by hand.\"\n}\n```\n\nWith `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude` configured and a successful read, the\nshape (per-hint field set, from `vision_bridge._FIELD_SPECS`) is:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"provider\": \"claude\",\n  \"available\": true,\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"odometer_km\": {\"value\": 142290, \"confidence\": 0.9, \"unit\": \"km\"}\n  },\n  \"suggested_kind\": null,\n  \"note\": \"Suggested from the photo -- confirm or correct every field before saving; this is not a car measurement.\"\n}\n```\n\nPer-hint field names and `suggested_kind` (the taxonomy `category/kind` the\nnative app should pre-select, or `null` when there is no single matching\none):\n\n| hint | fields | suggested_kind |\n|---|---|---|\n| `odometer` | `odometer_km` (number, km) | `null` -- goes on the event's own `odometer_km`, not a `fields` entry |\n| `fuel_pump` | `litres`, `price`, `octane`, `station` | `fuel/fill_up` |\n| `oil_bottle` | `brand`, `viscosity`, `qty` | `fluids/engine_oil_change` |\n| `part_label` | `part`, `part_no`, `brand` | `parts_repairs_elsewhere/part_fitted_elsewhere` |\n| `receipt` | `station`, `litres`, `price`, `at` | `fuel/fill_up` |\n| `other` | provider's best effort, unshaped | `null` |\n\nEach field value is `{\"value\": <reading or null>, \"confidence\": 0.0-1.0,\n\"unit\": <ours, never the model's, or null>}` -- a native app should treat\n`value: null` or low `confidence` as \"show the field empty, let the human\ntype it,\" never auto-accept.\n\n**Errors:** `400` for an unrecognised `hint` --\n\n```json\n{\"detail\": \"hint must be one of odometer, fuel_pump, oil_bottle, part_label, receipt, other, got 'bogus'\"}\n```\n\nA failed Claude call (network/HTTP error, or a non-JSON reply) is **not**\nan HTTP error -- it still returns `200` with `available: false` (or\n`available: true, fields: {}` for an unparseable reply) and a human-\nreadable `note`. A native app must branch on `available`/`fields`, not on\nHTTP status, to detect \"nothing to suggest.\"\n\n### Gap: `fields_meta` provenance is not yet wired to the API\n\n`cuore.live.owner_events.add()` now accepts a `fields_meta:\ndict[str, \"photo\"]` parameter (added 2026-10-13) that records, per field,\nwhether its value came from a photo read rather than being typed --\n`cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.add()` passes it straight through. **But\n`POST /api/owner/{vin}/events`'s request body (`OwnerEventRequest` in\n`cuore/api/owner_events.py`) has no `fields_meta` field yet** -- confirmed\nagainst the live schema (`components.schemas.OwnerEventRequest` in\n`app.openapi()` has no such property). A native app cannot, today, tell the\nserver \"this value came from a vision read\" when it saves the event; that\nprovenance is currently only reachable from the yet-to-be-updated web\n\"Snap & fill\" flow at the `cuore.web.owner_routes` layer, not the JSON API.\nRe-check this once `check_api_contract.py`'s next run shows\n`OwnerEventRequest` growing a `fields_meta` property, and update this gap\nnote (and the request example in [owner events](#owner-events-tell-cuore))\naccordingly.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":466,"oldLines":43,"newStart":466,"newLines":125,"lines":[" "," ---"," ","-## Vision (pending)","+## Vision"," ","-`/api/vision/*` **does not exist in the running schema** as of this","-document. It is specified, not built -- `docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md`","-(\"Mobile companion\", 2026-10-13):","+`/api/vision/*` is live. HTTP face of `cuore.services.vision_bridge`","+(\"pluggable 'read this photo' service for the mobile 'Tell CUORE' page\"),","+matching the roadmap note in `docs/handbook/06-roadmap.md` (\"Mobile","+companion\", 2026-10-13): *\"a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump","+proposing the fields for the human to confirm (pluggable vision provider,","+off by default because CUORE runs offline; the Claude provider is an","+explicit opt-in that sends the photo to Anthropic).\"*"," ","-> a photo of the odometer, oil bottle or pump proposing the fields for the","-> human to confirm (pluggable vision provider, off by default because CUORE","-> runs offline; the Claude provider is an explicit opt-in that sends the","-> photo to Anthropic).","+**Every value this returns is a suggestion, never a measurement, never","+written automatically.** This module never calls `POST","+/api/owner/{vin}/events` itself -- it only reads a photo already in hand","+(upload it separately via the media API if it should also be kept as","+evidence) and proposes field values for a human to confirm in the add-event","+form."," ","-`cuore/services/vision_bridge.py` does not exist yet either -- there is no","-docstring to transcribe. The contract a native app should build against,","-once it lands, follows the same shape as every other bridge in this file:","+### `GET /api/vision/status`"," ","-* **Provider is pluggable and off by default.** CUORE runs offline; no","-  photo leaves the device/LAN unless a vision provider is explicitly","-  configured. The documented provider is Claude, and selecting it is an","-  explicit opt-in because it sends the photo to Anthropic.","-* **Proposes, never commits.** The expected flow is upload a photo (via the","-  existing `POST /api/vehicles/{vin}/media`, `target_kind` likely","-  `\"vehicle\"` or a new `target_kind` for pump/odometer/bottle shots), then","-  call a vision endpoint that returns *proposed field values* (e.g.","-  `{\"odometer_km\": 142290, \"confidence\": \"proposed\"}`) for a human to","-  confirm or correct before anything is written to `owner_events`. It must","-  not call `POST /api/owner/{vin}/events` itself -- the human-confirm step","-  stays a distinct request, same as every other attested record in this","-  system (see [attested-record semantics](#attested-record-semantics)).","-* **Native app implication:** until this ships, camera capture on a native","-  app has nothing to call for auto-fill -- see","-  [native-only features](#native-only-features). Treat this section as the","-  spec to implement against, and re-run","-  `cuore/tests/check_api_contract.py` once `/api/vision/*` exists; it will","-  not fail for vision's absence (vision is not in the path table above),","-  but this document's \"pending\" language should be updated to match","-  whatever `app.openapi()` then reports.","+Which provider is configured, and whether it can actually be used *right","+now* -- never whether the last read succeeded."," ","+**Response 200** (default, no provider configured):","+","+```json","+{\"provider\": \"none\", \"available\": false, \"model\": null}","+```","+","+Three possible `provider` values: `\"none\"` (the default -- CUORE runs","+offline by rule; `available` is always `false`), `\"claude\"` (`available`","+reflects whether `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set server-side -- the photo is","+then sent to Anthropic's Messages API over the open internet, an explicit","+opt-in the owner turns on via `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude`, never the","+default), `\"tesseract\"` (a documented hook; always `available: false`","+today -- no OCR binary is wired up).","+","+### `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`","+","+**Params:** `vin` (path, accepted but not used to scope the read).","+**Body:** `multipart/form-data` -- `file` (the photo, required) and `hint`","+(form field, required, one of `odometer | fuel_pump | oil_bottle |","+part_label | receipt | other`).","+","+**Response 200**, provider `\"none\"` (today's default -- this is what a","+native app gets until an owner opts in to a provider):","+","+```json","+{","+  \"provider\": \"none\",","+  \"available\": false,","+  \"fields\": {},","+  \"suggested_kind\": null,","+  \"note\": \"Automatic reading is not set up on this CUORE. Fill in by hand.\"","+}","+```","+","+With `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER=claude` configured and a successful read, the","+shape (per-hint field set, from `vision_bridge._FIELD_SPECS`) is:","+","+```json","+{","+  \"provider\": \"claude\",","+  \"available\": true,","+  \"fields\": {","+    \"odometer_km\": {\"value\": 142290, \"confidence\": 0.9, \"unit\": \"km\"}","+  },","+  \"suggested_kind\": null,","+  \"note\": \"Suggested from the photo -- confirm or correct every field before saving; this is not a car measurement.\"","+}","+```","+","+Per-hint field names and `suggested_kind` (the taxonomy `category/kind` the","+native app should pre-select, or `null` when there is no single matching","+one):","+","+| hint | fields | suggested_kind |","+|---|---|---|","+| `odometer` | `odometer_km` (number, km) | `null` -- goes on the event's own `odometer_km`, not a `fields` entry |","+| `fuel_pump` | `litres`, `price`, `octane`, `station` | `fuel/fill_up` |","+| `oil_bottle` | `brand`, `viscosity`, `qty` | `fluids/engine_oil_change` |","+| `part_label` | `part`, `part_no`, `brand` | `parts_repairs_elsewhere/part_fitted_elsewhere` |","+| `receipt` | `station`, `litres`, `price`, `at` | `fuel/fill_up` |","+| `other` | provider's best effort, unshaped | `null` |","+","+Each field value is `{\"value\": <reading or null>, \"confidence\": 0.0-1.0,","+\"unit\": <ours, never the model's, or null>}` -- a native app should treat","+`value: null` or low `confidence` as \"show the field empty, let the human","+type it,\" never auto-accept.","+","+**Errors:** `400` for an unrecognised `hint` --","+","+```json","+{\"detail\": \"hint must be one of odometer, fuel_pump, oil_bottle, part_label, receipt, other, got 'bogus'\"}","+```","+","+A failed Claude call (network/HTTP error, or a non-JSON reply) is **not**","+an HTTP error -- it still returns `200` with `available: false` (or","+`available: true, fields: {}` for an unparseable reply) and a human-","+readable `note`. A native app must branch on `available`/`fields`, not on","+HTTP status, to detect \"nothing to suggest.\"","+","+### Gap: `fields_meta` provenance is not yet wired to the API","+","+`cuore.live.owner_events.add()` now accepts a `fields_meta:","+dict[str, \"photo\"]` parameter (added 2026-10-13) that records, per field,","+whether its value came from a photo read rather than being typed --","+`cuore/services/owner_events_bridge.add()` passes it straight through. **But","+`POST /api/owner/{vin}/events`'s request body (`OwnerEventRequest` in","+`cuore/api/owner_events.py`) has no `fields_meta` field yet** -- confirmed","+against the live schema (`components.schemas.OwnerEventRequest` in","+`app.openapi()` has no such property). A native app cannot, today, tell the","+server \"this value came from a vision read\" when it saves the event; that","+provenance is currently only reachable from the yet-to-be-updated web","+\"Snap & fill\" flow at the `cuore.web.owner_routes` layer, not the JSON API.","+Re-check this once `check_api_contract.py`'s next run shows","+`OwnerEventRequest` growing a `fields_meta` property, and update this gap","+note (and the request example in [owner events](#owner-events-tell-cuore))","+accordingly.","+"," ---"," "," ## Attested-record semantics"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"df8d92ae-ef42-4309-8679-cd086185a4de","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"beddb72a-7313-4205-9912-b0b1db5d2020","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
