{"parentUuid":"e1ae54c4-6195-49b5-bfbb-5b974f68a985","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfzuu7eTDgaJa2kt7KdAR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016SEqoyf7NBfSEkGQJasrzh","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md","old_string":"* A field proposed by a future vision call (above) is likewise never\n  committed as fact on its own -- it is a draft a human confirms, same as\n  anything typed by hand.","new_string":"* A field proposed by a `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` call (above) is\n  likewise never committed as fact on its own -- it is a draft a human\n  confirms, same as anything typed by hand. Once accepted, the intent is\n  for the saved event to stamp `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"` on that field\n  (`cuore.live.owner_events`'s own provenance convention) -- **informational\n  only**: a photo-read field is stored at the exact same `confidence:\n  \"reported\"` as a typed one, `fields_meta` just remembers *how* the value\n  got into the box. See the [vision gap note](#gap-fields_meta-provenance-is-not-yet-wired-to-the-api)\n  above: the JSON API does not yet accept `fields_meta` on `POST\n  /api/owner/{vin}/events`, so a native app cannot set this today even\n  though the store and bridge layers already support it."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3005,"cache_read_input_tokens":157240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3005,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016SEqoyf7NBfSEkGQJasrzh":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md","old_string":"* A field proposed by a future vision call (above) is likewise never\n  committed as fact on its own -- it is a draft a human confirms, same as\n  anything typed by hand.","new_string":"* A field proposed by a `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` call (above) is\n  likewise never committed as fact on its own -- it is a draft a human\n  confirms, same as anything typed by hand. Once accepted, the intent is\n  for the saved event to stamp `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"` on that field\n  (`cuore.live.owner_events`'s own provenance convention) -- **informational\n  only**: a photo-read field is stored at the exact same `confidence:\n  \"reported\"` as a typed one, `fields_meta` just remembers *how* the value\n  got into the box. See the [vision gap note](#gap-fields_meta-provenance-is-not-yet-wired-to-the-api)\n  above: the JSON API does not yet accept `fields_meta` on `POST\n  /api/owner/{vin}/events`, so a native app cannot set this today even\n  though the store and bridge layers already support it."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8ebddb1a-0770-4fa4-9948-5d0d7e773fcc","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cfzuu73jnjebqKmfbiVu7","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"84bae9b1-2f8c-4f89-a465-606abf88a723","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:03:05.518Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"84bae9b1-2f8c-4f89-a465-606abf88a723","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"32e1d820-4c02-417b-9eb5-eb28de0dd113","agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016SEqoyf7NBfSEkGQJasrzh","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"36b6f76b-1aeb-4cf6-9295-a676afcf0d70","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:03:05.901Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md","oldString":"* A field proposed by a future vision call (above) is likewise never\n  committed as fact on its own -- it is a draft a human confirms, same as\n  anything typed by hand.","newString":"* A field proposed by a `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` call (above) is\n  likewise never committed as fact on its own -- it is a draft a human\n  confirms, same as anything typed by hand. Once accepted, the intent is\n  for the saved event to stamp `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"` on that field\n  (`cuore.live.owner_events`'s own provenance convention) -- **informational\n  only**: a photo-read field is stored at the exact same `confidence:\n  \"reported\"` as a typed one, `fields_meta` just remembers *how* the value\n  got into the box. See the [vision gap note](#gap-fields_meta-provenance-is-not-yet-wired-to-the-api)\n  above: the JSON API does not yet accept `fields_meta` on `POST\n  /api/owner/{vin}/events`, so a native app cannot set this today even\n  though the store and bridge layers already support it.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":604,"oldLines":9,"newStart":604,"newLines":17,"lines":["   *caused* a code. A native app's UI copy must preserve this distinction","   (e.g. do not render \"Caused by: recent fill-up\"; render \"Reported around","   the same time: recent fill-up\").","-* A field proposed by a future vision call (above) is likewise never","-  committed as fact on its own -- it is a draft a human confirms, same as","-  anything typed by hand.","+* A field proposed by a `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read` call (above) is","+  likewise never committed as fact on its own -- it is a draft a human","+  confirms, same as anything typed by hand. Once accepted, the intent is","+  for the saved event to stamp `fields_meta[key] = \"photo\"` on that field","+  (`cuore.live.owner_events`'s own provenance convention) -- **informational","+  only**: a photo-read field is stored at the exact same `confidence:","+  \"reported\"` as a typed one, `fields_meta` just remembers *how* the value","+  got into the box. See the [vision gap note](#gap-fields_meta-provenance-is-not-yet-wired-to-the-api)","+  above: the JSON API does not yet accept `fields_meta` on `POST","+  /api/owner/{vin}/events`, so a native app cannot set this today even","+  though the store and bridge layers already support it."," "," The one existing pictogram/footer line every `/m/{vin}` page renders and"," that a native app should preserve in spirit:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8ebddb1a-0770-4fa4-9948-5d0d7e773fcc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"84bae9b1-2f8c-4f89-a465-606abf88a723","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"36b6f76b-1aeb-4cf6-9295-a676afcf0d70","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14839225 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c2d6819e-48c6-4b13-8a6e-b594afca1bb9","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:03:05.926Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14839225 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"c2d6819e-48c6-4b13-8a6e-b594afca1bb9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_016SEqoyf7NBfSEkGQJasrzh","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1603c651-48be-43bf-b99f-6952e909135c","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:03:08.599Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"1603c651-48be-43bf-b99f-6952e909135c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfzuufmyzsJpnEJfpqi89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now update the native-only features section item 2 (camera capture) since vision now exists rather than being pending."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":160245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dad0c342-225c-4434-b045-2b2975e06df7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfzuufWrXfHoJ8XrBDajb","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c4a16faa-e6ab-4a77-8883-17080fd780d8","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:03:08.598Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"c4a16faa-e6ab-4a77-8883-17080fd780d8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aac4b6645059d9774","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfzuufmyzsJpnEJfpqi89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LqSjTMnj2kZzEg1xC2G5qW","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\mobile\\API_CONTRACT.md","old_string":"2. **Camera capture -> `/api/vision` read.** Once vision lands (see\n   [Vision (pending)](#vision-pending)), a native app's camera capture\n   button is the natural trigger: snap a photo of the odometer/pump/oil\n   bottle, upload it, call the vision endpoint, show the proposed fields\n   for confirmation. The web page has no camera API to call from a browser\n   form in the same way, so this is a genuinely native-only interaction\n   even though the underlying write path is identical.","new_string":"2. **Camera capture -> `/api/vision` read.** `POST /api/vision/{vin}/read`\n   (see [Vision](#vision)) is live: a native app's camera capture button is\n   the natural trigger -- snap a photo of the odometer/pump/oil bottle,\n   call the vision endpoint with a `hint`, show the proposed fields for\n   confirmation, then save via `POST /api/owner/{vin}/events` (optionally\n   also keeping the photo as evidence via `POST\n   /api/vehicles/{vin}/media`). The web page has no camera API to call from\n   a browser form in the same way, so this is a genuinely native-only\n   interaction even though the underlying write path is identical. Remember\n   the provider is `\"none\"` (unavailable) until the owner explicitly\n   configures `CUORE_VISION_PROVIDER` server-side -- design the capture\n   flow so \"nothing was read, fill in by hand\" is a normal, expected\n   outcome, not an error state."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_